<title>CANADA: Frost may hit parts of Canada Prairies Sept 7-9.</title>
<headline>Frost may hit parts of Canada Prairies Sept 7-9.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's western and central Prairies were forecast to see a slight to moderate risk of frost Saturday, Sunday and Monday, Environment Canada said.</p>
<p>Moderate frost risks were forecast for those three mornings in the Peace River Valley and the northern Alberta grainbelt, Environment Canada's 10-day frost outlook said.</p>
<p>Slight frost risks were forecast for the rest of Alberta and Saskatchewan Saturday and Sunday with the risk extending into Manitoba's grainbelt Monday.</p>
<p>The Prairie's northern grainbelt faces a slight risk of frost Tuesday and Wednesday mornings.</p>
<p>A slight risk of frost was forecast for Alberta's foothills Sept 14 and 15.</p>
<p>-- Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548</p>
</text>
